window.docContents[244].resolve({"/Incompressible-Fluid-Mechanics/#PDEAtlas--Incompressible-Fluid-Mechanics--From-conservation-laws-to-incompressible-flow":{"contents":"Velocity and pressure are fields on space rather than labels attached permanently\nto individual particles. Pressure and viscosity transfer momentum between\nneighboring regions; an external body force adds momentum from outside the fluid.\nSobolev spaces and compactness enter for weak solutions, and energy estimates\ncontrol those solutions without automatically restoring smoothness.\n\n\n\n\n\n","context":"PDEAtlas\u0009Incompressible Fluid Mechanics","header":"8.1. From conservation laws to incompressible flow","id":"/Incompressible-Fluid-Mechanics/#PDEAtlas--Incompressible-Fluid-Mechanics--From-conservation-laws-to-incompressible-flow"}});